From: OpenWiFi BCM4360 Project <bcm4360@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] brcmfmac: chip: BCM4360 TCM rambase=0 and fixed RAM info

The BCM4360 ARM CR4 core maps TCM directly through BAR2 with no
offset: rambase must be 0 (BCM43602 uses 0x180000). Without this,
brcmf_chip_tcm_rambase() returns INVALID_RAMBASE and the probe fails
with "RAM base not provided with ARM CR4 core" before firmware
download. The chip's TCM is 640 KiB (0xa0000) with no separate SRAM.

Ported from kimptoc/bcm4360-re (reference/brcmfmac-reference/chip.c):
- brcmf_chip_tcm_rambase(): case BRCM_CC_4360_CHIP_ID -> 0
- brcmf_chip_get_raminfo(): early fixed-RAM branch for BCM4360
  (rambase=0, ramsize=0xa0000, srsize=0); kimptoc hardcodes these
  values because the CR4 bxinfo-derived ramsize is not reliable on
  this chip (D11 core rev 42, unusual memory layout).

Adaptation for 7.1.8: 7.1.8's get_raminfo() tail differs from
kimptoc's v6.12 base (7.1.8 uses brcmf_chip_socram_ramsize() and has
no SDRAM srsize subtraction), so the early-return branch is inserted
at the top of the function, before the memory-core lookup, keeping
the rest of the function byte-identical to upstream.

Signed-off-by: OpenWiFi BCM4360 Project <bcm4360@localhost>
---
 1 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 0 deletions(-)
diff --git a/brcmfmac/chip.c b/brcmfmac/chip.c
index 4adc0d0..8351f7b 100644
--- a/brcmfmac/chip.c
+++ b/brcmfmac/chip.c
@@ -723,6 +723,7 @@ static u32 brcmf_chip_tcm_rambase(struct brcmf_chip_priv *ci)
 	case BRCM_CC_43570_CHIP_ID:
 	case BRCM_CC_4358_CHIP_ID:
 	case BRCM_CC_43602_CHIP_ID:
+	case BRCM_CC_4360_CHIP_ID:
 	case BRCM_CC_4371_CHIP_ID:
 		return 0x180000;
 	case BRCM_CC_43465_CHIP_ID:
@@ -760,6 +761,17 @@ int brcmf_chip_get_raminfo(struct brcmf_chip *pub)
 	struct brcmf_core_priv *mem_core;
 	struct brcmf_core *mem;
 
+	if (ci->pub.chip == BRCM_CC_4360_CHIP_ID) {
+		/* BCM4360: TCM is 640 KiB mapped directly at BAR2, no
+		 * separate SRAM. The ARM CR4 bxinfo-derived size is not
+		 * reliable on this chip (D11 core rev 42), so use fixed
+		 * values (kimptoc phase5 test.121). */
+		ci->pub.rambase = 0;
+		ci->pub.ramsize = 0xa0000;
+		ci->pub.srsize = 0;
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	mem = brcmf_chip_get_core(&ci->pub, BCMA_CORE_ARM_CR4);
 	if (mem) {
 		mem_core = container_of(mem, struct brcmf_core_priv, pub);
--
2.39.2
